To me save scumming is to recover from death.  Been there, done that,
eventually learned that it does not work so I finally lost interest in
doing it.

So to me doing a backup to recover from a lost file is not save
scumming.  Almost everyone reports not losing a game to a deleted file
in several years of play.  The last time I lost a game to a computer
failure is so long ago that I stopped doing checkpoint backups years ago.

I don't know what you're doing to the files in the game directory but
whatever it is is very different from what most folks do.  I rarely even
delete bones files and I don't recall losing a game since Nethack 3.3.1
or before.  Do you have any idea what's going one that you lose files
when no one else seems to?


